System-Time: Tue 27 Jun 2000 16:21:38
To: <m.g-nospam@t-online.de>
From: Mark Richardson                                           
Subject: Re: emailit v1.5b

>>On 15Jun2000 at 21:09, Markus wrote:
>It's a nice and small program - I like it!
	Glad to hear that you like it.  It is 10 times smaller than PsiMail.

>And it works quicker as PsiMail!
	Yes I know.  About twice as fast!

>The sending works exellent, but when receiving my mail, it says "seq # bad" however I receive all mails...
	Most msgs displayed when TcpIp's debug facility is running are just diagnostic msgs; if they bother you, just turn off the debug facility.  Anything that is really important will most likely display on the screen.

>a little web-browser...  so small and so efficient like eMail-It!
	Not an easy task.  I plan to have a Telnet app which may be able to access the web via telnet.w3.org (CERN).  I am still not convinced the 3x/Siena has sufficient processing power to web browse in today's Internet.
	Perhaps someone will write a WAP browser using my TcpIp!

>At least I want to know where and when can I download the finished eMail-It v1.5?
	I hope to complete v2.0 (there will be no v1.5) in a few weeks.  It will be available at
 http://public.webbox.com/emailit@webbox.com

Mark
