System-Time: Tue 27 Jun 2000 08:08:56
To: emailit@webbox.com
Subject: 3c/mx email: eMail-it is great!
From: tph@mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk (Tony Hodge)
Date: Tue, 27 Jun 2000 09:05:28 +0100
Organization: MRC-LMB
User-Agent: MacSOUP/2.4 (unregistered for 440 days)

[ A copy of this message has been posted to the newsgroup ]
[     comp.sys.psion.comm                                 ]

Just wanted to voice my support for Mark Richardson's eMail-It app for the 3/Sienna series.  I had tried to make a connection to Freeserve using PMI but with no joy (Thanks Ro for the help and advice) and was about to have another go when I decided to give eMail-It a try.  It was only then that I found out it has its own TCP/IP stack and I did not need PMI.  If all you need is email - try this!

I had problems with PMI and Freeserve even with Ro Cutlers prv files and some help from him by email.  I could get so far with the connection but it never completed.  I was beginning to suspect my home made null modem adapter and that was my next target to attack the problem.

However using eMail-It 1.4 I just entered the settings for Freeserve and off it went sending and receiving mail with no problems.  I have also set it up for my Free NTL account but I don't get a connection every time using my Mac with this service and have not fully tested it.

I found setting up eMail-It to be quite straight forward (especially following the README file) and much less 'arcane' than PMI.

Mark - if you can develop the TCP/IP side to allow other apps to use it for eg HTML that would be a winner.

settings info in case it helps:

Version used: 1.4, Psion 3mx, Motorola 3400 modem.

  Std Modem Settings:   
     Baud rate:          38.4k
     Parity:              none
     Data bits:            8
     Stop bits:            1
     Handshaking:         RTS
     Ignore DSR:           Y

Well done Mark, do you have a website?

tony
