	A guy is in a hot air balloon, enjoying himself, until he realizes he is lost.
	He lowers the balloon to about 30 feet above the ground and calls out to the first person he sees, "Hey buddy! Do you know where I am?"  "Sure," comes the reply, "you are about 30 feet above the ground in a hot air balloon."
	The balloonist replied, "You are a computer guy!  Only a computer guy would give me an answer that is 100 percent correct but also 100 percent useless!"
	"Oh yeah," said the computer guy.  "You must be an end-user.  You don't know where you are or where you are going, but suddenly it's all my fault!"
